description: Project conventions for InventarioWeb
globs:
  - "src/**/*.{ts,tsx}"
  - "supabase/**/*"
alwaysApply: true
---

# Product direction

- Build a Spanish-language, responsive internal article register.
- Keep the React/TypeScript frontend separate from the legacy WPF desktop application.
- Preserve local demo mode when either Supabase variable is missing. Label it “Demo local” and persist its data in the browser.
- The article table has exactly four columns: Nombre, Categoría, Fecha de ingreso, Acciones (Ver, Editar, Borrar).

# Architecture and quality

- Keep UI components presentational where practical; persistence belongs in `src/lib/inventoryRepository.ts` and demo fixtures in `src/data/demo.ts`.
- Keep database snake_case mapping at the repository boundary. Use shared camelCase models from `src/types.ts`.
- Validate required values and duplicate internal codes. Show useful Spanish errors; do not swallow backend errors.
- Set entry dates on creation: database `created_at` default or the current system time in demo.
- Keep keyboard focus, semantic labels, and reduced-motion support intact.

# Supabase security

- Use only `VITE_SUPABASE_URL` and `VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` in browser code.
- Never put service-role keys, secrets, or passwords in frontend code, `.env.example`, commits, or logs.
- Enable RLS on exposed tables and enforce row ownership in Postgres, not only in React filters.
- The global Auth user count is available only through the JWT-protected Edge Function and only to callers with `app_metadata.role = "admin"`.
- Keep SQL changes under `supabase/`; review RLS and grants before applying them remotely.

# Workflow

- Pin dependencies and keep the package lockfile synchronized.
- Run `npm run build` after TypeScript or UI changes.
- When layout or visual tokens change, update `docs/figma-brief.md`.
- Do not commit secrets, generated build output, or `node_modules`.
